  "verbalization": "Latifoloside A is shown to have a target relationship with ME-180 through multiple pathways, with the strongest evidence linking Latifoloside A to ME-180 via DSH1. DSH1 is identified as a target of both Latifoloside A and of Oblongifolin C, which in turn targets ME-180. This suggests that Latifoloside A may exert its effects through DSH1, which is a key player in the signaling pathways leading to ME-180. Additionally, Latifoloside A is also shown to target DSH1 directly, reinforcing the notion that it may act through this enzyme. The evidence is consistent across different pathways, indicating that Latifoloside A may influence ME-180 through a shared target, DSH1, which is involved in multiple biological processes. The relationship is supported by multiple layers of evidence, but the exact mechanism by which Latifoloside A interacts with DSH1 to affect ME-180 remains to be fully elucidated.",
